nel-3_18`  Change-Id: I750a96cb986b5c54e9f4da46d86390071a8530b3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356346 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356346" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/46/356346/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I397ddf69b555c07af6263d53fe606ed362fb6a29" commit="695111c100780512e78db3e6042ca6c17bb61854" commit_message="BACKPORT: mwifiex: scan: replace pointer arithmetic with array access  improves readability  Reviewed-by: Julian Calaby &lt;julian.calaby@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Andreas Fenkart &lt;afenkart@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kalle Valo &lt;kvalo@codeaurora.org&gt; (cherry-pick from commit 948ad6b34943a1247653392d59bcfc9896da8fe7  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/kvalo/wireless-drivers-next.git  master) [wnhuang: backport due to directory changes]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53795 TEST=`emerge-oak chromeos-kernel-3_18`  Change-Id: I397ddf69b555c07af6263d53fe606ed362fb6a29 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356347 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356347" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/47/356347/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I22828f11a72ba73b4b50524c3ec71f9496fce2c5" commit="0590ee67f8231d2f435058300c97ecd4f4e6fb09" commit_message="BACKPORT: mwifiex: factor out mwifiex_cancel_pending_scan_cmd  Releasing the scan_pending lock in mwifiex_check_next_scan_command introduces a short window where pending scan commands can be removed or added before removing them all in mwifiex_cancel_pending_scan_cmd. I think this is safe, since the worst thing to happen is that a pending scan cmd is removed by the command handler. Adding new scan commands is not possible while one is pending, see scan_processing flag. Since all commands are removed from the queue anyway, we don't care if some commands are removed by a different code path earlier, the final state remains the same. I assume, that the critical section needed for the check has been extended over clearing the pending scan queue out of convenience. The lock was already held and releasing it and grab it again was just more work. It doesn't seem to be necessary because of concurrency.  Signed-off-by: Andreas Fenkart &lt;afenkart@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kalle Valo &lt;kvalo@codeaurora.org&gt; (cherry-pick from commit c70ca8cb9a7c6722d5bb6d428b6571921998c48d  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/kvalo/wireless-drivers-next.git  master) [wnhuang: backport due to directory changes]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53795 TEST=`emerge-oak chromeos-kernel-3_18`  Change-Id: I22828f11a72ba73b4b50524c3ec71f9496fce2c5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356342 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356342" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/42/356342/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I93a6088bfe4958feb7f430fdc0842647992958e6" commit="e2239b8