m.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356321" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/21/356321/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I3befdefb0b70c9ffab848508f837e3db4a97b70d" commit="c86802888367128eac9a178db6db0f423d6a2bc1" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Allow Android to set RT scheduler.  When running in the android container, Android needs to set RT scheduler for some of its services.  Setting RT scheduler affects the host so process inside container needs to have privilege targeted the host to achieve that.  However this is not configurable nor supported by kernel, so we use alt-syscall to provide Android the needed functionality.  BUG=b:29250079 TEST=check thread prio while running audio from Android on Minnie.  Change-Id: I3befdefb0b70c9ffab848508f837e3db4a97b70d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354351 Commit-Ready: Chinyue Chen &lt;chinyue@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chinyue Chen &lt;chinyue@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354351" owner_email="chinyue@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/354351/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I011757bb3773a9a191b2b130022eb904430a4706" commit="210263229d53eeaa6c7956ef977bb364cce4b489" commit_message="umpire: check and raise exception if client info has multi-line data.  When creating connection to Umpire, the client will first send &quot;UmpireClientInfo&quot; as X-UMPIRE-DUT HTTP Header, and will cause problem if that has multiple line data.  It is possible to solve this by quoting header line first, but all fields used here are also expected to not having newline in other APIs (for example, many shopfloor APIs using serial_number as param would fail if the serial number contains newline character).  So we are not changing the Umpire DUT line, but there will be an additional check to help people find out what goes wrong.  BUG=none TEST=make test  Change-Id: I011757bb3773a9a191b2b130022eb904430a4706 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356289 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356289" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/89/356289/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6a7f2e2b8392eb3ac6f738216bb9d8224eddaf79" commit="96f77c79bfd6a813f14ae130cfe53773fc32f18b" commit_message="Add name of new signal handler to dbus constants.  BUG=b:29342389 TEST=None  Change-Id: I6a7f2e2b8392eb3ac6f738216bb9d8224eddaf79 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356223 Commit-Ready: Dan Spaid &lt;dspaid@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Spaid &lt;dspaid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yoshiki Iguchi &lt;yoshiki@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="356223" owner_email="dspaid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/system_api" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/system_api" ref="refs/changes/23/356223/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia24d2445121583766f19a2cd19b6229919c7a615" commit="4001a89be80a9bec5feb67b442ceeea132297285" commit_message="i